ite, early spring blossom is prone to frost damage and protection is usually needed.  It may set some fruit on its own, but it benefits significantly from cross-pollination with another Japanese plum to set good crops. Cropping season: July","image":"_KOS0361.jpg","commonName":"plum 'Shiro'","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":132216,"synonymParentPlantName":"<em>Prunus</em> 'Shiro' (D)","isAgm":false,"isSynonym":true,"isPlantsForPollinators":true,"price":null},{"id":14030,"botanicalName":"<em>Prunus</em> <em>serrulata</em> 'Hokusai'","entityDescription":"A vigorous, wide-spreading tree with bronze foliage which changes to green as it matures then to brown, orange and red in the autumn.  Large clusters of semi-double, highly fragrant pale pink flowers which turn almost white, smother the branches in the spring","image":"RHSPG055.jpg","commonName":"cherry 'Hokusai'","nurseriesCount":14,"synonymParentPlantId":97245,"synonymParentPlantName":"<em>Prunus</em> 'Hokusai'","isAgm":true,"isSynonym":true,"isPlantsForPollinators":false,"price":{"plantId":97245,"price":"£140.24","oldPrice":null,"url":"https://www.rhsplants.co.uk/plants/_/prunus-hokusai/classid.2000048981/sku.TR30000912/"}},{"id":307471,"botanicalName":"<em>Prunus</em> <em>spinosa</em> 'Rosea'","entityDescription":"Rounded, deciduous tree about 10m tall, with slender purple stems bearing bronze-purple young leaves, becoming bronze-green then green in late summer. Small, salmon-pink flowers, crowd the stems and fade with age, open in early and mid-spring with the leaves and may be followed by dark red, edible, plum-like fruit","image":"visi27568.jpg","commonName":"blackthorn 'Rosea'","nurseriesCount":0,"synonymParentPlantId":47607,"synonymParentPlantName":"<em>Prunus</em> <em>cerasifera</em> 'Rosea'","isAgm":false,"isSynonym":true,"isPlantsForPollinators":true,"price":null},{"id":96915,"botanicalName":"<em>Prunus</em> <em>tenella</em>","entityDescription":"A species of small, slow-growing, upright deciduous